1870:#### Environment Variables
1871-
1872-- `env(key)`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Retrieves the environment variable with name `key`, aborting
1873-  if it is not present.
1874-
1875-```just
1876-home_dir := env('HOME')
1877-
1878-test:
1879-  echo "{{home_dir}}"
1880-```
1881-
1882-```console
1883-$ just
1884-/home/user1
1885-```
1886-
1887-- `env(key, default)`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Retrieves the environment variable with
1888-  name `key`, returning `default` if it is not present.
1889-- `env_var(key)` — Deprecated alias for `env(key)`.
1890-- `env_var_or_default(key, default)` — Deprecated alias for `env(key, default)`.
1891-
1892-A default can be substituted for an empty environment variable value with the
1893-`||` operator, currently unstable:
1894-
1895-```just
1896-set unstable
1897-
1898-foo := env('FOO', '') || 'DEFAULT_VALUE'
