2333-| Name | Type | Description |
2334-|------|------|-------------|
2335-| `[arg(ARG, help="HELP")]`<sup>1.46.0</sup> | recipe | Print help string `HELP` for `ARG` in usage messages. |
2336-| `[arg(ARG, long="LONG")]`<sup>1.46.0</sup> | recipe | Require values of argument `ARG` to be passed as `--LONG` option. |
2337-| `[arg(ARG, pattern="PATTERN")]`<sup>1.45.0</sup> | recipe | Require values of argument `ARG` to match regular expression `PATTERN`. |
2338-| `[arg(ARG, short="S")]`<sup>1.46.0</sup> | recipe | Require values of argument `ARG` to be passed as short `-S` option. |
2339-| `[arg(ARG, value="VALUE")]`<sup>1.46.0</sup> | recipe | Makes option `ARG` a flag which does not take a value. |
2340-| `[confirm(PROMPT)]`<sup>1.23.0</sup> | recipe | Require confirmation prior to executing recipe with a custom prompt. |
2341-| `[confirm]`<sup>1.17.0</sup> | recipe | Require confirmation prior to executing recipe. |
2342-| `[default]`<sup>1.43.0</sup> | recipe | Use recipe as module's default recipe. |
2343-| `[doc(DOC)]`<sup>1.27.0</sup> | module, recipe | Set recipe or module's [documentation comment](#documentation-comments) to `DOC`. |
2344-| `[dragonfly]`<sup>1.47.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on DragonFly BSD. |
2345:| `[env(ENV_VAR, VALUE)]` <sup>1.47.0</sup> | recipe | Set environment variables for recipe. |
2346-| `[extension(EXT)]`<sup>1.32.0</sup> | recipe | Set shebang recipe script's file extension to `EXT`. `EXT` should include a period if one is desired. |
2347-| `[exit-message]`<sup>1.39.0</sup> | recipe | Print error message if recipe fails regardless of `set no-exit-message`. |
2348-| `[freebsd]`<sup>1.47.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on FreeBSD. |
2349-| `[group(NAME)]`<sup>1.27.0</sup> | module, recipe | Put recipe or module in [group](#groups) `NAME`. |
2350-| `[android]`<sup>1.50.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on Android. |
2351-| `[linux]`<sup>1.8.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on Linux. |
2352-| `[macos]`<sup>1.8.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on macOS. |
2353-| `[metadata(METADATA)]`<sup>1.42.0</sup> | recipe | Attach `METADATA` to recipe. |
2354-| `[netbsd]`<sup>1.47.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on NetBSD. |
2355-| `[no-cd]`<sup>1.9.0</sup> | recipe | Don't change directory before executing recipe. |
2356-| `[no-exit-message]`<sup>1.7.0</sup> | recipe | Don't print an error message if recipe fails. |
2357-| `[no-quiet]`<sup>1.23.0</sup> | recipe | Override globally quiet recipes and always echo out the recipe. |
2358-| `[openbsd]`<sup>1.38.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on OpenBSD. |
2359-| `[parallel]`<sup>1.42.0</sup> | recipe | Run this recipe's dependencies in parallel. |
2360-| `[positional-arguments]`<sup>1.29.0</sup> | recipe | Turn on [positional arguments](#positional-arguments) for this recipe. |
2361-| `[private]`<sup>1.10.0</sup> | alias, recipe | Make recipe, alias, or variable private. See [Private Recipes](#private-recipes). |
2362-| `[script(COMMAND)]`<sup>1.32.0</sup> | recipe | Execute recipe as a script interpreted by `COMMAND`. See [script recipes](#script-recipes) for more details. |
2363-| `[script]`<sup>1.33.0</sup> | recipe | Execute recipe as script. See [script recipes](#script-recipes) for more details. |
2364-| `[unix]`<sup>1.8.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on unixes. (Includes macOS). |
2365-| `[windows]`<sup>1.8.0</sup> | recipe | Enable recipe on Windows. |
2366-| `[working-directory(PATH)]`<sup>1.38.0</sup> | recipe | Set recipe working directory. `PATH` may be relative or absolute. If relative, it is interpreted relative to the default working directory. |
